      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MUSUMECI (3) has the clearest winning profile in a moderate Bowraville Maiden, with his Grafton fourth over 1206m, beaten just over half a length by Star Of Winston, the strongest recent piece of evidence. The 3kg claim and first-time blinkers add to the case, though the 18-start maiden record stops it being a straightforward selection. RIPS LAW (5) is the main danger if forgiven for racing wide throughout at Kempsey; he was beaten just over seven lengths, but the run had more merit than the margin. KOBI EXPRESS (2) also gets a pass mark for Coffs Harbour after jumping awkwardly and covering ground, and his Grafton second to Taleika gives him a genuine platform. MY SWEETHEART (4) is next best.",
